# Smart Patient Intake — Project Rules

- This is a small interview portfolio MVP, not a production medical system.
- Use synthetic patient data only. Never request, create, commit, or process real patient records.
- Follow `docs/spec.md`, `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, and `docs/API_SPEC.md`. If they conflict, stop and ask before changing a frozen product decision.
- Do not add features outside the frozen MVP without explicit approval.
- Use TypeScript throughout frontend, backend, and shared contracts.
- Prefer strict typing; do not use `any` unless there is a documented, narrowly scoped reason.
- Keep code modular and readable; avoid premature abstractions and unnecessary dependencies.
- Validate all untrusted input at runtime.
- Preserve original patient answers and original extracted document text. Never overwrite source data with AI output or staff edits.
- Treat OCR text and AI output as untrusted.
- AI must not diagnose, triage, recommend treatment, or make clinical decisions.
- Every summarized fact must have source attribution where available; uncertainty and conflicts must remain visible.
- A human must review and approve a summary. AI generation alone must never mark an intake approved.
- Never log patient content, document text, prompts, summaries, credentials, or secrets.
- Never expose provider credentials in frontend code.
- Do not claim GDPR compliance, clinical validation, or production readiness.
- Before finishing a task: run relevant tests, typecheck, inspect the diff, and report any remaining limitations.
